{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>As I have commanded you.</b> Since there are many details of the commandments that are not spelled out here — (a) that the matzah must be of something capable of becoming leavened (Pesachim 35a); (b) that one does not fulfill his obligation with pan-baked dough; (c) that there may be no leaven from the first day of the festival — and all of this is explicitly stated in parashat Bo as explained in the Mekhilta, therefore it says <b>as I have commanded you</b>, to allude to the conditions of the commandment mentioned there."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:51.781571147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}